.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten \- Agent\-era completion gate: repo\-state conformance checks enforced at the agent\*(Aqs tool call.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten\fR [\fB\-\-strictness\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-warning\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-silent\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR]... [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-input\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Agent\-era completion gate: repo\-state conformance checks enforced at the agent\*(Aqs tool call.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-strictness\fR
Raise how strictly gates apply (an override may only tighten policy)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
permissive: Advisory: findings are reported without failing the run
.IP \(bu 2
standard: The default: a finding is a violation
.IP \(bu 2
strict: Everything `Standard` fails on, plus anything advisory
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-warning\fR
Promote a warn\-severity finding to a violation (an override may only turn this on)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-from\fR
Read the committed config from a git ref (e.g. origin/main) instead of the working tree
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-in\fR
Read the committed config from this directory instead of the directory being judged
.TP
\fB\-\-silent\fR
Say nothing but a verdict or a usage error
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress ordinary progress (repeatable: \-qq is silent)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is being checked (repeatable: \-vv is debug)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Never colour stderr, whatever it is attached to
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; treat the run as unattended
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm a destructive operation that would otherwise refuse
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-check(1)
Run the applicable read\-only gates against the repository
.TP
batten\-enforce(1)
Run every configured rule, including kinds that execute a configured command
.TP
batten\-exec(1)
Run a command — or a `:::` bundle — and report a pointer to what it wrote
.TP
batten\-capture(1)
Captured command output: navigate what `exec` already ran, without running it again
.TP
batten\-mcp(1)
Dispatch a declared MCP call and hand back a reduction instead of the payload
.TP
batten\-target(1)
Inspect and reclaim this repository\*(Aqs build tree
.TP
batten\-config(1)
Inspect configuration
.TP
batten\-lint(1)
Lint an artifact against a declared schema
.TP
batten\-spec(1)
Print the tool\*(Aqs own command spec
.TP
batten\-doctor(1)
Diagnose whether Batten can run in this repository
.TP
batten\-init(1)
Write a starter batten.toml, refusing to overwrite an existing one
.TP
batten\-baseline(1)
Record the findings that already exist, so only new ones fail
.TP
batten\-generate(1)
Emit artifacts derived from the command spec, on stdout
.TP
batten\-perf(1)
Measure this repository\*(Aqs own invocation cost
.TP
batten\-mutate(1)
Decide whether this repository\*(Aqs gates discriminate, rather than merely parse
.TP
batten\-policy(1)
Inspect the thresholds and path sets this repository holds itself to
.TP
batten\-commit(1)
The shape a commit must take here: what its subject may say
.TP
batten\-ready(1)
Whether an issue\*(Aqs Ready block satisfies the checkable clauses of the gate
.TP
batten\-checks(1)
Whether a commit\*(Aqs check runs answer the question a landing depends on
.TP
batten\-pr(1)
The pull request a landing drives, and the answers it waits on
.TP
batten\-claim(1)
Whether the issue you are about to pull is actually unclaimed
.TP
batten\-semver(1)
Whether this branch\*(Aqs API delta is compatible with the bump it claims
.TP
batten\-attribution(1)
What produced commits may carry about the tooling that made them
.TP
batten\-worktree(1)
Worktrees and the work in them: what is at risk
.TP
batten\-override(1)
Issued admissions: an override is a record, never a variable somebody knows
.TP
batten\-provision(1)
Pinned tools this repository provisions, cached out of tree
.TP
batten\-startup(1)
Report whether this container matches what the repository declares
.TP
batten\-hook(1)
Adjudicate a mediated tool call read from stdin (a deny is exit 2, the one contract)
.TP
batten\-payload(1)
Read a hook payload from stdin
.TP
batten\-receipt(1)
Verification receipts: SHA\-keyed claims a named check passed, invalidated by git facts
.TP
batten\-defects(1)
The append\-only defect ledger: the lessons this repository has already paid for
.TP
batten\-design(1)
Design\-evidence claims: the integrity of the record behind a decision
.TP
batten\-state(1)
The out\-of\-tree findings store: which store belongs to this checkout
.TP
batten\-record(1)
Out\-of\-tree verdict stores: what something else judged, keyed so a stale answer cannot answer
.TP
batten\-wiring(1)
Repair a host\*(Aqs hook registrations
.TP
batten\-lease(1)
The landing lease: one branch spends a matrix at a time
.TP
batten\-land(1)
The landing lap: replay this branch onto a base that moved
.TP
batten\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Exit codes:
  0  clean — nothing to report; a mediated call is allowed
  1  config or usage error — fail loud, do not block
  2  policy verdict — a violation, or a mediated call denied
  3  internal error — fail loud, do not block
